      ],
      "outcome": "success",
      "exception": null,
      "narration": "Nicco's fist catches Livia Marr square across the jaw. She staggers back, pins scattering from her lips to the wooden floor, her hand flying to her face as her measuring tape swings wildly at her collar. For a moment she stares at him, dark-blond hair slipping from its pins, eyes wide with shock rather than pain still settling in.\n\nThen her expression hardens. \"Out.\" Her voice comes tight, controlled, the blunt energy of her manner compressed into something flat and final. She does not touch him, does not move toward him, but her small frame blocks the path deeper into the shop, toward the bolts of linen and the alteration tables. \"Get out of my shop. Now.\" She spits a fleck of blood onto her palm and looks at it, then back at him, waiting.",
